WEBVTT

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.600
(FEMALE ANNOUNCER
ANNOUNCING ON PA)

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.280
-(ALARM BLARING)
-(GRUNTS IN FRUSTRATION)

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.280
Step aside, sir. Random security check.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:52.440
Random my behind!
You always stop me.

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:54.760
I'm just a surge protector
doing my job, sir.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:56.560
-Name?
-Lara Croft.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.240
-Name?
-Wreck-It Ralph!

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.760
And where are you coming from?

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:01.200
Uh... Pac-Man.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:02.720
Did you bring any fruit with you?

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:04.280
No! No. No fruit.

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:05.720
Okay, then. Where are you heading?

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:06.840
Fix-It Felix Jr.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:08.720
-Anything to declare?
-I hate you.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:10.600
I get that a lot. Proceed.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:16.680
-Bad guy coming!
-(SCREAMING)

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.040
SONIC: If you leave your game,

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:22.080
stay safe, stay alert,

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:24.520
and whatever you do, don't die.

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.800
Because if you die
outside your own game

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.400
you don't regenerate.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:30.240
Ever. Game over.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:41.480
Here you go, buddy.

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:45.680
It's fresh. Straight from Pac-Man's.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.240
Hang in there, guys.

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:48.800
-(ALARM BLARING)
-Name?

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:50.240
(GRUNTS IN FRUSTRATION)

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:52.040
(DANCE MUSIC PLAYING) (DANCE MUSIC PLAYING)

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.520
Celebrate good times
Come on!

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:07.640
(BELL RINGING)

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:13.680
(FIREWORKS EXPLODING)

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:16.280
(FIREWORKS WHISTLING)

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:27.000
"Happy 30th Anniversary"?

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:29.400
They're having a party without me.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.920
Pac-Man? They invited Pac-Man?

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.440
That cherry-chasing dot-muncher

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:38.920
isn't even part of this game!

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:40.800
Great party, Felix.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:42.240
Why, thank you, friend.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:44.240
Felix. You're needed on the dance floor!

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:47.440
(WHOOPING)

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:49.280
ALL: Whoo!

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:54.200
NICELANDERS: Fix-It Felix!
Whoo-whoo! Fix-It Felix!

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:55.800
(DOORBELL RINGS)

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.040
Oh! I'll bet that's Mario.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:59.440
Fashionably late, per the norm.

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:01.080
I'll get it, Felix.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:02.480
(HUMMING)

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.840
-Ahh!
-(MUSIC STOPS)

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:07.880
It's Ralph!

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:09.080
(SCREAMING)

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.160
-He'll wreck the party!
-Hide the stemware!

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:12.240
Get rid of him, Felix.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:15.040
Oh, right. I'll go talk to him.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:16.680
Carry on, everyone.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.480
(MUSIC STARTS AGAIN)

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:20.640
Ralph, can I help you?

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.560
Hey, Felix.
Just wanted to check on you.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.600
I saw a big explosion

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:27.000
or something go over the building there.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:29.800
Oh, those were just fireworks.

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:31.320
Fireworks. Okay. Phewf.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:33.120
Somebody's birthday, or...

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:37.440
Well, it's more of an anniversary.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:40.120
The 30th anniversary
of our game, actually.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.160
What? Is that today?

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:43.400
I know!

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:44.920
I'm such a dummy with dates.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:47.280
Anyway, uh, congratulations.

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:50.520
Thank you, Ralph. And to you, too.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.440
-(CHUCKLES)
-(CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY)

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:56.240
Uh...

00:03:58.080 --> 00:03:59.520
Hi. Just a heads-up, Felix.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:00.640
They're bringing out the cake
in a few shakes.

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:03.520
-Hey, Glen.
-Ralph.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:07.680
Cake? Heard about this cake stuff.
(CHUCKLES)

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:08.960
Never had it.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.440
No one ever seems to throw it out

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:11.600
so it never ends up in the dump.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.440
I never actually tasted it. Uh...

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:17.240
I've always wanted to try cake.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:20.120
I don't suppose you'd like to

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:21.720
come in and have a slice, would you?

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:24.240
Hey-o, everybody! Oh!

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:25.480
Ah!

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:27.880
(ALL GASP)

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:32.720
I'm okay. I'm okay. Fit as a fiddle.

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:34.640
(ALL EXHALING)

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:36.640
-Now, you all know Ralph.
-Evening.

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:37.720
(ALL GASP)

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:41.200
Evening, Nell, Lucy, Don, Dana...

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.120
-Deanna.
-RALPH: Big Gene!

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:44.560
Why is he here?

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:46.840
He's just here for a slice of cake.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:48.720
And I'm a big part of the game,

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:50.320
technically speaking.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:52.080
Why are you here, Gene?

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:53.640
Oh, look! The cake!

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:54.760
(GASPS)

00:04:55.720 --> 00:05:00.120
Well, I'll be dipped. You've
really outdone yourself, Mary.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.640
NORWOOD: Oh, and look!
There's all of us at the top.

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:06.080
Each apartment
is everyone's favorite flavor.

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:07.840
Norwood's is red velvet.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:08.920
NORWOOD: Guilty!

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:12.440
And lemon for Lucy, rum cake for Gene,

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:14.040
-and for Felix...
-Hey, Mary.

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:15.440
Um...

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:18.680
What's the flavor of that mud
that I'm stuck in there?

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:21.640
Hmm? Oh. Chocolate.

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:24.240
I've never been real fond of chocolate.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:26.160
Well, I did not know that.

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:27.480
One other little thing.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:31.080
I hate to be picky,
but this angry little guy here...

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:33.120
-My cake!
-...might be a lot happier

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:35.600
if you put him up here
with everyone else.

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:37.840
See that? Look at that smile.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.000
No, no. You see, Ralph,

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:42.200
there's no room for you up here.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:45.760
(CHUCKLES) What about this?
We can make room.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.560
Here. We could take turns. Easy.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:49.680
(ALL GASP)

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:51.520
How about we just eat the cake?

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:54.000
Hang on. Felix needs to be on the roof

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:56.040
because he's about to get his medal!

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:58.400
Then how about we just take that medal

00:05:58.480 --> 00:05:59.840
and give it to Ralph for once?

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:01.520
Would that be
the end of the world, Gene?

00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:03.360
Now you're just being ridiculous.

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:05.160
Only good guys win medals,

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.800
and you, sir, are no good guy.

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:09.360
I could be a good guy if I wanted to,

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:10.520
and I could win a medal!

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:13.480
Uh-huh. And when you do,
come and talk to us.

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:16.320
Then would you finally let me be
on top of the cake with you guys?

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:17.440
If you won a medal,

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:19.440
we'd let you live
up here in the penthouse!

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:21.480
But it will never happen

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:24.640
because you're just the bad guy
who wrecks the building.

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:26.320
No, I'm not.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:27.520
Yes, you are!

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:29.320
No, I'm not!

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:30.920
(ALL EXCLAIM)

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:32.040
(GASPS)

